│ +# PORT VESPER
│ +
│ +An original top-down open-world crime game for make.fun gta6-01. The whole game is plain static
│ +files under `game/`: no build step, no packages, no external assets and no network requests.
│ +Everything you see and hear is drawn on a canvas or synthesised with WebAudio at runtime.
│ +
│ +## Play
│ +
│ +```
│ +node serve.ts
│ +```
│ +
│ +Open the local address the server prints. The game starts on a title screen.
│ +
│ +| Control | Action |
│ +| --- | --- |
│ +| WASD or arrow keys | Walk; W/S accelerate and brake while driving, A/D steer |
│ +| Shift | Sprint on foot |
│ +| Mouse | Aim |
│ +| Click | Shoot |
│ +| Space | Enter the nearest car or get out |
│ +| E | Start or advance a job at the glowing marker |
│ +| P or Escape | Pause |
│ +| M | Mute |
│ +| C | Continue from the title screen |
│ +| R | Clear the saved game from the title screen |
│ +
│ +## The city
│ +
│ +Port Vesper is a hand-authored seven-by-six street grid with sidewalks, tower blocks, shop rows,
│ +a park, an open market, a waterfront and a pier. Civilian cars follow the lanes and turn at
│ +junctions, pedestrians walk the pavements and scatter when the heat is on, and police cars appear
│ +as your wanted level climbs from one to five stars.
│ +
│ +Three jobs are available in order: deliver a parcel from a lot to the pier, crack the safe at
│ +Vesper Market, then shake the police and reach the safehouse. Completing jobs pays cash, refills
│ +ammo and unlocks the next one. Progress, money, health and position are kept in localStorage.
│ +
│ +## Screenshot modes
│ +
│ +The game can stage its own deterministic frames for the four captures:
│ +
│ +```
│ +?shot=start&seed=7
│ +?shot=street&seed=7
│ +?shot=chase&seed=7
│ +?shot=mission&seed=7
│ +```
│ +
│ +Each mode starts from a fresh seeded world, runs a fixed number of simulation steps with scripted
│ +input, paints twice and sets `window.__shotReady`. The same seed always yields the same frame.
│ +
│ +## Source layout
│ +
│ +```
│ +game/index.html       page and canvas
│ +game/src/config.js    tuning, palette and city constants
│ +game/src/world.js     the authored grid, buildings, lane rules and collision helpers
│ +game/src/entities.js  cars, pedestrians, bullets and particles
│ +game/src/mission.js   the three mission state machines
│ +game/src/input.js     keyboard and pointer
│ +game/src/audio.js     synthesised sound
│ +game/src/render.js    camera, city drawing, HUD and screens
│ +game/src/shots.js     deterministic screenshot plans
│ +game/src/game.js      simulation, boot and localStorage save
│ +```
│ +
